gfx: WINDOW_ONLY, a window with gfx's input, events, time and draw-on-demand wait,
and no GPU device, for another renderer to draw into (Draughts' ngfx build, task 065).

open(..., WINDOW_ONLY) makes the window and no SDL_GPU device; native_window() gives
its native handle (a CAMetalLayer from an SDL Metal view on Apple's systems, the HWND on
Windows, the ANativeWindow on Android; none headless). The renderer calls presented()
each frame with whether it showed one; a frame() after one that showed nothing waits
for an event as gfx's own frames do (0002), and needs_present() says the window was
exposed, shown or resized, so the renderer presents again. screen_size() is the window's
size in pixels. Every call that needs the device is a misuse in this mode.

To propose upstream (goose_gfx): gfx as the platform for another renderer, the run-time
choice of renderer opening the window first.

